WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.283 --> 00:00:01.969
- Welcome to Mom vs. Chef!

00:00:01.969 --> 00:00:03.881
- [Andrew] A competition
where a professional chef

00:00:03.881 --> 00:00:06.176
and a mom cook head-to-head, preparing the

00:00:06.176 --> 00:00:08.622
best dish possible, featuring
one secret ingredient.

00:00:08.622 --> 00:00:09.455
(swishing)

00:00:09.455 --> 00:00:11.911
(driving rock music)

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.804
Our first competitor today
is mom, Tahara Christie.

00:00:14.804 --> 00:00:16.364
- Most people don't even
know I have four kids.

00:00:16.364 --> 00:00:17.339
They meet me, and then they're like,

00:00:17.339 --> 00:00:18.297
"oh, my gosh, you're super fun!"

00:00:18.297 --> 00:00:19.412
I'm like, "I know, right?"

00:00:19.412 --> 00:00:20.913
My grandmother taught me how to cook.

00:00:20.913 --> 00:00:21.793
There were no recipes.

00:00:21.793 --> 00:00:24.833
She'd be like, "oh, you know,
you put it in 'til it browns."

00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:27.515
I'm a little intimidated.

00:00:27.515 --> 00:00:30.294
'Cause, you know, I'm
competing against a top chef!

00:00:30.294 --> 00:00:31.285
But, you know what?

00:00:31.285 --> 00:00:32.993
I'm from Oakley, California, baby.

00:00:32.993 --> 00:00:34.910
Nothing intimidates us!

00:00:36.098 --> 00:00:38.746
Winning Mom vs. Chef will make me the best

00:00:38.746 --> 00:00:41.579
non-trained mom-chef in the world!

00:00:43.598 --> 00:00:44.648
- And competing against her is

00:00:44.648 --> 00:00:46.967
professional chef Dakota Weiss.

00:00:46.967 --> 00:00:49.408
- I've been cooking
professionally for 18 years,

00:00:49.408 --> 00:00:52.287
and I'm the chef-partner
at Estrella Restaurant,

00:00:52.287 --> 00:00:55.167
and chef-partner at Sweetfin
Poké in Santa Monica.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.628
Growing up, my mom really inspired me

00:00:56.628 --> 00:00:59.468
to become the chef that
I am, kinda forced us

00:00:59.468 --> 00:01:01.568
to eat organic and
vegetables, and everything

00:01:01.568 --> 00:01:02.411
out of the garden.

00:01:02.411 --> 00:01:05.793
Cooking against a mom who
actually cooks for children daily

00:01:05.793 --> 00:01:07.093
is a little nerve-wracking.

00:01:07.093 --> 00:01:10.370
I have to kinda dig deep
into my inner child.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.834
Winning this competition
would be great, just love

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:14.435
for my niece and nephew to watch it,

00:01:14.435 --> 00:01:16.475
and be really excited for Aunt Kota.

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.418
- [Andrew] Welcome Tahara, Chef Weiss.

00:01:18.418 --> 00:01:20.192
Today, you're gonna be
competing against each other,

00:01:20.192 --> 00:01:22.424
trying to create the
tastiest dish possible,

00:01:22.424 --> 00:01:25.583
featuring one secret ingredient
in 30 minutes or less.

00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:27.344
Your dishes will be judged by the

00:01:27.344 --> 00:01:28.773
panel of judges before you.

00:01:28.773 --> 00:01:29.606
- My name's Elijah.

00:01:29.606 --> 00:01:31.847
I am 10 years old, and I want to become

00:01:31.847 --> 00:01:34.158
a pro-baseball player or soccer player.

00:01:34.158 --> 00:01:35.389
- I'm Sydni Sepulveda.

00:01:35.389 --> 00:01:37.463
I'm 12 years old, and when
I grow up, I would love

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:38.871
to be an actor and singer.

00:01:38.871 --> 00:01:40.092
- And your final judge is me.

00:01:40.092 --> 00:01:42.192
I'm Andrew; I'm 25 years old.

00:01:42.192 --> 00:01:46.153
And, when I grow up, I wanna
be a maple syrup farmer.

00:01:46.153 --> 00:01:47.676
I think it's time to find out what our

00:01:47.676 --> 00:01:49.993
secret ingredient is.

00:01:49.993 --> 00:01:51.879
Sydni, want to take the lid off for us?

00:01:51.879 --> 00:01:53.520
- Sure.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.122
(laughs)

00:01:55.122 --> 00:01:56.484
- You guys know what kind of fish this is?

00:01:56.484 --> 00:01:57.317
- No.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.826
- Different types, I'm guessing.

00:01:58.826 --> 00:02:01.028
- No, it's all one kind of fish.

00:02:01.028 --> 00:02:02.102
- [Elijah] Oh, wow.

00:02:02.102 --> 00:02:03.171
- Guys, this is salmon.

00:02:03.171 --> 00:02:05.674
- I have a lot of experience
cooking with salmon.

00:02:05.674 --> 00:02:08.116
I've burnt plenty of
pieces, but I've learned

00:02:08.116 --> 00:02:10.655
that, if you broil it and do it quickly,

00:02:10.655 --> 00:02:13.076
it can come out really good
and tasty on the inside.

00:02:13.076 --> 00:02:15.297
- When I eat salmon,
I really like it to be

00:02:15.297 --> 00:02:17.417
a little chewy, but not too chewy.

00:02:17.417 --> 00:02:19.397
- I don't like the raw fish taste.

00:02:19.397 --> 00:02:20.230
- Alright.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.181
I've cooked a lot with salmon.

00:02:21.181 --> 00:02:23.022
It's one of those fishes that really goes

00:02:23.022 --> 00:02:24.661
in a lot of different cuisines.

00:02:24.661 --> 00:02:27.102
It's so versatile; it's just
a really great piece of fish.

00:02:27.102 --> 00:02:28.663
- So, guys, you're gonna have 30 minutes

00:02:28.663 --> 00:02:30.144
to prepare your dishes.

00:02:30.144 --> 00:02:31.610
Your time starts now.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:32.503
(beeping)

00:02:32.503 --> 00:02:33.609
(rock and roll music)

00:02:33.609 --> 00:02:34.766
- [Tahara] Think.

00:02:34.766 --> 00:02:35.599
Think.

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:37.991
- I'm still kinda conceptualizing
my dish in my head.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:40.674
So, what I wanna do a play on a carpaccio,

00:02:40.674 --> 00:02:42.653
which is thinly sliced salmon with some

00:02:42.653 --> 00:02:44.533
nice citrus and avocado.

00:02:44.533 --> 00:02:46.533
Thinking I wanna do a good play on, maybe,

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.993
introducing some raw fish, and then also

00:02:48.993 --> 00:02:51.113
doing some cooked fish, as well.

00:02:51.113 --> 00:02:53.054
- A lot of people have
missed the boat when it comes

00:02:53.054 --> 00:02:55.274
to salmon, 'cause they
just think: lemon, dill,

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:57.261
salt-pepper. Boring!

00:02:57.261 --> 00:02:59.699
I'm gonna make this delicious, sweet glaze

00:02:59.699 --> 00:03:00.740
on top of it.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.673
I wanna make, like, an egg
roll and then everything

00:03:02.673 --> 00:03:03.723
will have vegetables in it.

00:03:03.723 --> 00:03:06.179
- I haven't really used
these pre-made sauces before,

00:03:06.179 --> 00:03:07.918
so it should be interesting.

00:03:07.918 --> 00:03:08.987
Some fresh peanut butter.

00:03:08.987 --> 00:03:11.268
- Kids like mustard; they like hot dogs.

00:03:11.268 --> 00:03:14.068
Soy sauce, some butter, brown sugar.

00:03:14.068 --> 00:03:16.989
Chow! They ain't even
gonna know what hit 'em.

00:03:16.989 --> 00:03:18.849
- [Dakota] Sounds like you
got quite the plan over there.

00:03:18.849 --> 00:03:20.107
- I don't get how they cut like that!

00:03:20.107 --> 00:03:21.992
- [Elijah] I know they go
like this. (mouth noises)

00:03:21.992 --> 00:03:23.334
- [Dakota] Kids like
sweet things, don't they?

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:25.255
- [Tahara] Kids love
sweet, they love crunchy.

00:03:25.255 --> 00:03:27.056
I see the carrots; I see the shredder,

00:03:27.056 --> 00:03:28.797
and I start shredding my vegetables.

00:03:28.797 --> 00:03:31.757
I want to incorporate lots of
vegetables so it's healthy,

00:03:31.757 --> 00:03:33.997
but not so many that it's overpowering.

00:03:33.997 --> 00:03:36.577
- I really wanna make sure
that my salmon carpaccio

00:03:36.577 --> 00:03:38.417
is palatable.

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:42.137
I pound it out as thin as I possibly can.

00:03:42.137 --> 00:03:45.157
Maybe this might be a nice
introduction into sushi.

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:47.679
- I see that there's an
extra piece of meat there,

00:03:47.679 --> 00:03:48.939
and I'm like, ooh, ground beef.

00:03:48.939 --> 00:03:50.099
Kids really like ground beef.

00:03:50.099 --> 00:03:51.640
Let me just throw that in there, as well.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.587
- [Dakota] I put a
little maldon salt on it,

00:03:54.587 --> 00:03:57.118
and, kinda try to build
that part of the dish.

00:03:57.118 --> 00:03:59.685
I'm a little nervous,
you know, doing raw fish

00:03:59.685 --> 00:04:01.650
for kids is definitely a little risky.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:03.850
(laughs) So, I don't know
how this is gonna go.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:05.269
I may have gone too fancy.

00:04:05.269 --> 00:04:06.299
I dunno.

00:04:06.299 --> 00:04:09.375
- I'm so focused I forget
to cut the salmon up,

00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:12.575
because I was just so excited
to get it in the oven.

00:04:12.575 --> 00:04:15.294
While that's cooking, then
I start making my noodles.

00:04:15.294 --> 00:04:17.416
- Whoo, she's got all kinds
of things cooking over there,

00:04:17.416 --> 00:04:19.968
and I don't have anything
on the stove yet.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.117
- [Andrew] Chefs you have 15 minutes left.

00:04:21.117 --> 00:04:22.317
- 15 minutes.

00:04:22.317 --> 00:04:23.333
- [Dakota] Heard.

00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:24.557
- Fifteen minutes!

00:04:24.557 --> 00:04:26.231
- [Dakota] Now, I'm gonna pull the salmon

00:04:26.231 --> 00:04:28.438
out of the marinade and skewer them.

00:04:28.438 --> 00:04:31.137
Every kid I know, they all
love anything you can eat

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:32.118
off of a stick.

00:04:32.118 --> 00:04:33.392
- My noodles! Oh!

00:04:33.392 --> 00:04:34.360
- She's really focused.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.081
- Delicious meal from
the momma that loves 'em.

00:04:38.081 --> 00:04:39.922
Your momma loves you, baby.

00:04:39.922 --> 00:04:41.482
As I wait for my salmon to come out,

00:04:41.482 --> 00:04:44.583
I then start preparing my
rice paper for the rolling.

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.123
- [Andrew] I think she's making something

00:04:46.123 --> 00:04:47.224
a little bit spicy, guys.

00:04:47.224 --> 00:04:48.057
- Yeah, it looks spicy.

00:04:48.057 --> 00:04:48.890
I like spicy food.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.482
- I've just started
getting into spicy foods.

00:04:50.482 --> 00:04:51.544
- [Elijah] It's like a wrap.

00:04:51.544 --> 00:04:52.377
- [Andrew] A spring roll? Yeah.

00:04:52.377 --> 00:04:54.025
- [Sydni] Yeah, like a wrap, maybe?

00:04:54.025 --> 00:04:54.955
It looks really good.

00:04:54.955 --> 00:04:57.114
Hey, Elijah, let's go
check in Chef Dakota.

00:04:57.114 --> 00:04:57.947
- Okay, let's go.

00:04:57.947 --> 00:04:59.400
- I'll check on Chef Tahara.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.233
- Hey, Chef Dakota.

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.066
- How's it going?

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:01.899
- Good!

00:05:01.899 --> 00:05:02.732
- This looks good.

00:05:02.732 --> 00:05:03.640
So, what're you making?

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:05.961
- Kinda doing a play on a
cooked and a raw salmon.

00:05:05.961 --> 00:05:08.901
- What is the sauce you're
dipping the fish in?

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:12.923
- This is a coconut-peanut
sauce, a play on a satay.

00:05:12.923 --> 00:05:14.123
- Yeah.

00:05:14.123 --> 00:05:15.139
- Thank you Chef Dakota.

00:05:15.139 --> 00:05:16.147
- Thanks!

00:05:16.147 --> 00:05:17.335
- Hey, Tahara, how's it going?

00:05:17.335 --> 00:05:18.168
- Good, good, good.

00:05:18.168 --> 00:05:20.747
Just trying to get the
last little bits in here.

00:05:20.747 --> 00:05:22.549
- I see you've been trying
a couple different ways

00:05:22.549 --> 00:05:23.388
of making your dish.

00:05:23.388 --> 00:05:26.171
- I've just spanded the whole globe.

00:05:26.171 --> 00:05:28.252
I think it's gonna be
fried, so it doesn't matter,

00:05:28.252 --> 00:05:29.085
it'll be delicious.

00:05:29.085 --> 00:05:31.109
- This doesn't exactly
look like salmon to me.

00:05:31.109 --> 00:05:33.510
- There's definitely salmon in it.

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:35.449
Kids who don't necessarily
eat fish all the time,

00:05:35.449 --> 00:05:37.309
they can always be thrown off by meat.

00:05:37.309 --> 00:05:39.489
Let's just say I've got
many cultures going on

00:05:39.489 --> 00:05:40.408
at the same time.

00:05:40.408 --> 00:05:42.076
- I'm really looking forward to it.

00:05:42.076 --> 00:05:42.909
- Thank you.

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:44.479
I'm normally not this messy at home.

00:05:44.479 --> 00:05:46.249
I've got a little sous
chef I gave birth to.

00:05:46.249 --> 00:05:47.650
- I am normally this messy.

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:48.869
(laughs)

00:05:48.869 --> 00:05:49.850
- Five minutes left, chefs.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:50.858
- Whoo!

00:05:50.858 --> 00:05:51.691
- [Tahara] Add a little bit of this.

00:05:51.691 --> 00:05:54.331
I realize that it's time for
me to take my salmon out.

00:05:54.331 --> 00:05:57.500
It looks delicious; it's
the right type of flaky.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.772
But, realizing that I forgot to cut it up,

00:05:59.772 --> 00:06:02.991
I now have to cut the
salmon right in the middle,

00:06:02.991 --> 00:06:05.932
so it looks like a big ol' hunk
of meat on top of the plate.

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:07.472
But, I know it's gonna be delicious,

00:06:07.472 --> 00:06:08.412
so that won't even matter.

00:06:08.412 --> 00:06:10.932
- And now, I take my peanut-coconut milk

00:06:10.932 --> 00:06:13.632
and I dress that salmon, and
it looks really beautiful.

00:06:13.632 --> 00:06:15.652
The colors are bright and I'm very happy.

00:06:15.652 --> 00:06:16.952
- I'm completely confident.

00:06:16.952 --> 00:06:19.292
I put some of the salmon
on top of that plate,

00:06:19.292 --> 00:06:22.391
and with, literally, five seconds left,

00:06:22.391 --> 00:06:23.290
(countdown starts)

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:25.204
I throw my chives on top of the plate.

00:06:25.204 --> 00:06:26.037
And viola!

00:06:27.563 --> 00:06:29.597
- Zero! (laughs)

00:06:29.597 --> 00:06:31.746
- [Andrew] Time is up.

00:06:31.746 --> 00:06:34.078
- Tahara, please explain your dish.

00:06:34.078 --> 00:06:37.411
- I have made a brown sugar honey salmon

00:06:38.321 --> 00:06:40.042
on top of rice noodles.

00:06:40.042 --> 00:06:42.109
It's got some green onions,
it's got a little bit

00:06:42.109 --> 00:06:43.238
of ground beef.

00:06:43.238 --> 00:06:46.825
Like a beef-vegetable-carrot-empanada

00:06:46.825 --> 00:06:49.570
salmon-roll-bake thing.

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:50.403
- This looks good!

00:06:50.403 --> 00:06:51.357
- Looks beautiful!

00:06:51.357 --> 00:06:54.756
I love how you placed the
fish on top of the pasta.

00:06:54.756 --> 00:06:57.089
The fish glaze looks really good.

00:06:57.089 --> 00:06:59.421
(crunching)

00:06:59.421 --> 00:07:00.946
- First, when I saw it, I'm like, whoa.

00:07:00.946 --> 00:07:03.184
It reminds me of going
to the seafood restaurant

00:07:03.184 --> 00:07:05.823
with my family on my birthday.

00:07:05.823 --> 00:07:07.230
- I love how you put the ground beef

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.830
with the vegetables inside of it.

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:10.932
It brought out so many
more flavors in salmon

00:07:10.932 --> 00:07:12.072
than I thought there were.

00:07:12.072 --> 00:07:13.594
You really did surprise me.

00:07:13.594 --> 00:07:17.154
- The beef texture is a
little bit rough on my gums.

00:07:17.154 --> 00:07:18.756
- Elijah, did you get a bone there?

00:07:18.756 --> 00:07:19.822
- Yep.

00:07:19.822 --> 00:07:21.449
- Oops!

00:07:21.449 --> 00:07:24.562
- It's a really unique
combination of things.

00:07:24.562 --> 00:07:27.402
I don't think it reminds me
of any specific one cuisine,

00:07:27.402 --> 00:07:28.423
but I really like it.

00:07:28.423 --> 00:07:30.928
- Thank you, Tahara, for your dish.

00:07:30.928 --> 00:07:32.966
- Chef Dakota, can you
please describe your dish?

00:07:32.966 --> 00:07:34.784
- So, what I did for you
is a play on two different

00:07:34.784 --> 00:07:35.617
kinds of salmon.

00:07:35.617 --> 00:07:38.268
The first is a carpaccio-style,
and I glazed it

00:07:38.268 --> 00:07:41.495
with some soy, sesame,
vinaigrette, a little fresh

00:07:41.495 --> 00:07:45.411
blood orange, avocado, sesame
seeds, and a Thai basil.

00:07:45.411 --> 00:07:49.251
And then, I also did a
salmon satay pop in a classic

00:07:49.251 --> 00:07:51.493
coconut-peanut sauce on top of a little

00:07:51.493 --> 00:07:53.934
sauteed shiitake and some snap peas.

00:07:53.934 --> 00:07:56.534
- I love your presentation,
but I would've liked

00:07:56.534 --> 00:07:58.335
the soy sauce to be even
on both sides 'cause I'm

00:07:58.335 --> 00:07:59.955
very particular with stuff.

00:07:59.955 --> 00:08:01.538
(laughs)

00:08:01.538 --> 00:08:02.455
- Be brave!

00:08:04.028 --> 00:08:04.861
- Wow.

00:08:04.861 --> 00:08:07.190
I can really taste the blood orange in it.

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:09.005
- I love the avocado on
top, that really added

00:08:09.005 --> 00:08:10.626
a nice touch to it.

00:08:10.626 --> 00:08:13.569
- This dish makes me wanna
run to the beach right now.

00:08:13.569 --> 00:08:15.235
Just make a sand angel.

00:08:15.235 --> 00:08:16.068
I love it!

00:08:16.068 --> 00:08:18.591
- I definitely love the
peanut-coconut sauce.

00:08:18.591 --> 00:08:21.912
I think the soy sauce
with the sesame seeds

00:08:21.912 --> 00:08:23.843
is a little too sour for me.

00:08:23.843 --> 00:08:26.074
For now, I think I'm gonna
stick with cooked salmon.

00:08:26.074 --> 00:08:27.675
- It is really just like butter.

00:08:27.675 --> 00:08:29.813
I mean, this is how I love to eat fish.

00:08:29.813 --> 00:08:31.479
- Thank you, Chef Dakota, for your dish.

00:08:31.479 --> 00:08:32.312
- Absolutely.

00:08:32.312 --> 00:08:34.230
- This is gonna be a hard deliberation.

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:35.779
- Mine was just kinda like spaghetti.

00:08:35.779 --> 00:08:36.612
(laughs)

00:08:36.612 --> 00:08:38.743
Meat! Work! And it did!

00:08:38.743 --> 00:08:40.287
- It did! I thought it was gorgeous.

00:08:40.287 --> 00:08:41.120
- Thank you!

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.808
- What do you guys think
about Tahara's dish?

00:08:42.808 --> 00:08:46.441
- I would prefer the beef to
be a little bit less chalky.

00:08:46.441 --> 00:08:48.710
- I didn't like the
ground beef in the pasta.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.531
- Was I the only person
that got a bone in mine?

00:08:50.531 --> 00:08:51.592
- You were the only
person that got a bone.

00:08:51.592 --> 00:08:52.425
- I didn't get a bone,

00:08:52.425 --> 00:08:54.478
but I think she was just
a little rushed for time.

00:08:54.478 --> 00:08:56.739
- Honestly wanted to steal
every secret that you had.

00:08:56.739 --> 00:08:57.977
And, while I like you,
and we should have wine

00:08:57.977 --> 00:08:59.689
together some day, you're goin' down.

00:08:59.689 --> 00:09:00.522
(laughs)

00:09:00.522 --> 00:09:01.688
Just wanted you to
know; you're goin' down.

00:09:01.688 --> 00:09:02.964
- As much as I think you're fabulous,

00:09:02.964 --> 00:09:05.384
I'd be horribly embarrassed
if I lost to you,

00:09:05.384 --> 00:09:08.363
I can't go back to my kitchen
and tell all my cooks,

00:09:08.363 --> 00:09:09.968
Yeah, sorry, guys.

00:09:09.968 --> 00:09:11.479
So, yeah, I wanna win this.

00:09:11.479 --> 00:09:12.312
- Chef Dakota.

00:09:12.312 --> 00:09:13.145
- Yes.

00:09:13.145 --> 00:09:14.024
- I've had salmon a lot of ways.

00:09:14.024 --> 00:09:15.564
I've never had it as a Popsicle.

00:09:15.564 --> 00:09:16.730
- Yeah.

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:18.363
- [Andrew] That was really cool.

00:09:18.363 --> 00:09:19.196
What a contrast!

00:09:19.196 --> 00:09:21.769
- Yeah, it went back to
when we were three or four,

00:09:21.769 --> 00:09:23.863
and we would just eat
Popsicles out on the porch.

00:09:23.863 --> 00:09:25.308
- I still eat Popsicles out on my porch.

00:09:25.308 --> 00:09:26.141
(laughs)

00:09:26.141 --> 00:09:26.974
- I do, too.

00:09:26.974 --> 00:09:27.807
- Yeah, same her.

00:09:27.807 --> 00:09:28.940
- It reminds me of when I was little.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:30.860
- This was a really hard decision, but --

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:32.221
- I think we all know who won.

00:09:32.221 --> 00:09:33.858
- Let's call the contestants back out.

00:09:33.858 --> 00:09:34.741
(playful music)

00:09:34.741 --> 00:09:36.368
- Chef Dakota, Tahara, welcome back.

00:09:36.368 --> 00:09:37.628
Thank you both for coming in today,

00:09:37.628 --> 00:09:39.794
you both cooked some amazing dishes.

00:09:39.794 --> 00:09:43.531
- Tahara, your brown
sugar-honey-salmon glaze

00:09:43.531 --> 00:09:45.114
was really amazing.

00:09:45.114 --> 00:09:48.173
- Chef Dakota, your
salmon Popsicle stood out.

00:09:48.173 --> 00:09:51.334
- The winner of Mom vs. Chef is...

00:09:51.334 --> 00:09:52.167
- Chef Dakota!

00:09:52.167 --> 00:09:53.357
(Cries out, clapping)

00:09:53.357 --> 00:09:54.236
(laughs)

00:09:54.236 --> 00:09:55.779
- Whoo-hoo! (laughs)

00:09:55.779 --> 00:09:57.123
- I can't believe I lost.

00:09:57.123 --> 00:10:00.801
Honestly, this is what this girl does,

00:10:00.801 --> 00:10:02.881
so I didn't want to hurt her too bad,

00:10:02.881 --> 00:10:05.321
so I probably held back just a little bit.

00:10:05.321 --> 00:10:06.160
- It's quite the honor.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.364
It really is, honestly.

00:10:07.364 --> 00:10:09.804
I know kids' palettes can be very finicky,

00:10:09.804 --> 00:10:11.764
cooking for my niece and
nephews, so this is good!

00:10:11.764 --> 00:10:13.284
I'm real excited to tell my sister,

00:10:13.284 --> 00:10:15.083
and my niece and nephew, this is awesome.

00:10:15.083 --> 00:10:16.230
- Thank you both for coming in,

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:18.450
and cooking some amazing food for us.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:19.612
This has been Mom vs. Chef.

00:10:19.612 --> 00:10:21.159
What do you guys want for dessert?

00:10:21.159 --> 00:10:22.053
Fish Popsicle?

00:10:22.053 --> 00:10:25.277
- How 'bout we just stick with
chocolate cake or something?

00:10:25.277 --> 00:10:27.077
- Yeah, we could do chocolate cake.

00:10:27.077 --> 00:10:29.577
(dance music)

00:10:32.426 --> 00:10:34.343
- [Voiceover] Oh, yes!

